}
```
This is exactly the mobile styles but without changing layout. But at width 844, minimap right91, interact right1, no overlap. Good. It's a compact control set. On desktop short (1440x600) controls smaller than usual, fine.

Let's do that. Remove transform, set sizes. At height 390, controls bottom6 height112 → top272. Stats top143 height148=291; overlap with interact top? interact bottom4, container bottom6 → button bottom 380, top304; no overlap with stats 291. Good. Minimap bottom8 → y314..382, x? right91 width106 → x647..753, no overlap with button x? right1 width76 → x767..843? Wait container right = 844-23=821 desktop, button right1 → x744..820; minimap x647..753 overlaps 744..753 (9px). Hmm desktop controls right23, minimap right139 in base -> right edge 705, not 753. Wait if we only set minimap right91 in short media, then x = 844-91-106=647, right=753. Button x=744..820, overlap 9px. We could set minimap right:100px or interact button right:0 and minimap right:90; overlap. In mobile media, controls left/right12, minimap right91, width106 → x193? For 390 width: x=390-91-106=193..299; interact right1 within controls right12 → right 389, width76 →313..389. Gap 14. Fine because container right12 not23. For desktop/short, container right23; button x744..820, minimap x647..753 overlap 9. Set short minimap right:105px → right 739, gap 5. Or set button right:0 and minimap right:100. Let's set `.minimap{right:104px}` in short media. At width 844: x634..740, button x744..820, gap 4. Good.

But also stats x699..825 and minimap x634..740 no overlap vertical? Stats ends291; minimap y314+ no. fine.

Set sizes. This duplicates mobile CSS; acceptable.

Alternatively we can use `zoom` on controls? no.

